<title>DENMARK: Danish February unemployment falls to 8.1 percent.</title>
<headline>Danish February unemployment falls to 8.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted unemployment was 8.1 percent of the workforce in February 1997, down from  a revised 8.2 percent in January, the National Statistics Office said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>				 Feb 199  7    Jan 1997   Feb 1996</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate     8.1 pct	*8.2 pct   *9.2 pct</p>
<p>    Total unemployed     226,000	 *229,700   *274,900</p>
<p>*Revised All above figures seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>NOTE - A panel of economists polled by Reuters had on average forecast seasonally adjusted February year-on-year unemployment of 8.2 percent. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652.</p>
</text>
